<!--
Rendered into the Story description as markdown. Delete this comment when
rendering.

Four required sections, in this order: the opening statement, then the
Acceptance criteria, Test plan and Dependencies headings. Keep all four and
fill them, using "None" where that is the honest answer.

The opening statement has no heading. Jira already labels the field
Description, and "As a / I want / So that" says what it is, so a "User story"
heading above it only repeats the frame.

When no real person is in the sentence (a refactor, a migration, a platform
change), open with a goal instead: one sentence saying what is true afterwards
and why it matters, also with no heading. "As a developer, I want OrderService
split" is filler shaped like a user story. "OrderService is split into pricing
and persistence, so a pricing change deploys without a database migration" is
a goal.

Every other heading is optional. Drop an optional heading entirely when it has
no content. An empty optional heading is noise, and a story carrying eight
headings for two facts is why the last batch was unreadable.

There is no word cap. Say everything the implementer needs that the code and
the epic do not already say, and cut the padding rather than the content. The
prose rules, the banned punctuation and the placeholder rules are in the
issue-writing reference.
-->

